From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:51:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 68/92] Input: melfas_mip4 - use the resolution of one axis for
 the other

Some firmwares report the resolution of one axis only (the MMS438 of the
Galaxy J4 reports 10 for X and nothing for Y), and libinput refuses such a
device as a kernel bug, so no compositor gets touch events. The sensor
cells are square, so use the one value for both.

Signed-off-by: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0dcca69fe6ea0f14e153e65b0a133e360af0d7df)
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
index a6946e3d8..878fc9d41 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
@@ -333,6 +333,15 @@ static int mip4_query_device(struct mip4_ts *ts)
 
 		ts->ppm_x = buf[12];
 		ts->ppm_y = buf[13];
+
+		/*
+		 * Some firmwares report the resolution of one axis only, which
+		 * libinput rejects as a kernel bug. The sensor has square cells.
+		 */
+		if (!ts->ppm_x)
+			ts->ppm_x = ts->ppm_y;
+		if (!ts->ppm_y)
+			ts->ppm_y = ts->ppm_x;
 		dev_dbg(&ts->client->dev, "ppm_x: %d, ppm_y: %d\n",
 			ts->ppm_x, ts->ppm_y);
 
